      {
        "position": 1,
        "title": "Amazing first aid kit for both humans and dogs!",
        "text": "With the addition of a new furry friend to our family we felt we needed to be better prepared for the potential dangers that the great outdoors present to the dog. Although pricey - we did fork over the money to buy this robust medical supply. And don't let the title fool you - this kit is PERFECTLY equipped to deal with human injury as well. So much so that we feel comfortable leaving behind our own first aid kit which we've packed for 10 years. We are active in the outdoors spending most weekends during any given summer camping in dispersed camping sites throughout the US national forests and park systems and with that - plenty of potential scenarios for our little pup to get herself in trouble. And this kit has come in handy it's fair share of times already.By far the most valuable part of this is the field guide to K9 first aid. Reading through it gives you a great knowledge of what to do in emergency situations if you're not near an emergency vet. I could see it being an invaluable resource in the event of an emergency and have referenced it several times to understand what our options are and how best to treat a given situation that we've encountered (swollen face from being stung, removing ticks and treating a pretty nasty attack of black fly bites).I feel very confident that we can handle anything we come up against with our four legged family member when equipped with this first aid kit. Well worth the money for the peace of mind we now have when traveling in unknown areas around the country. I would highly recommend!",
